diff --git a/apps/mobile/assets/app-icon/README.md b/apps/mobile/assets/app-icon/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..9100f6543
--- /dev/null
+++ b/apps/mobile/assets/app-icon/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Bot app icon
+
+The shipped iOS/Android icon is a raster of our own generated artwork (icon C),
+not the SVGs in this folder and not a trace of another app's icon.
+
+Source still (QA only, not shipped in the IPA): the generated icon-C JPEG in the review compare folder.
+
+Pipeline: crop to a full-bleed square (drop the white margin), fill the baked
+rounded-corner wedges so iOS can mask the corners itself (three black corners,
+bottom-left continues the cream body), and clear any leftover light sliver
+where the body meets the left edge. The 1024 master is opaque RGB.
+
+Copied from `ios-sizes/icon-1024.png` into:
+
+- `../bot-icon.png`, `../icon.png` — 1024 master
+- `../adaptive-icon.png`, `../Bot.icon/Assets/bot-foreground.png` — body on a transparent field
+- `../monochrome-icon.png`, `../notification-icon.png`, `../favicon.png` — white silhouette, eyes punched out
+- `../icon-background.png` — solid black
+- `../splash-icon.png`, `../splash-icon-dark.png` — full-bleed icon
+
+`Bot.icon/icon.json` fill is black (`extended-srgb:0,0,0,1`).
+
+`bot-icon.svg`, `bot-icon-foreground.svg`, and `bot-icon-mono.svg` are earlier
+hand-drawn sketches. They are not the shipped icon. Safe to keep in the repo.
+
+The display name is **Bot**. Do not put "rakazo" or a third-party mark on the
+artwork.
